-     entry .cardinality   checks a numeric literal against its bounded type as the code compiles
-         The `FromDigits` given which makes `val x: 0.0 ~ 1.0 = 0.2` typecheck; it needs
-         `scala.language.experimental.genericNumberLiterals`. A literal below the lower bound
-         is error `↯/s.16.4`, _the value `v` is less than the lower bound for this value, `min`_, and
-         one above the upper bound error `↯/s.16.3`, _the value `v` is greater than the upper bound for
-         this value, `max`_; bounds which are not `Double` literal types are errors `↯/s.16.1` and `↯/s.16.2`.
-         Both bounds are inclusive.
+           Класс given-экземпляра `.cardinality`; его собственный `fromDigits` преобразует без
